<h2>Creating Amazon EC2 Instances</h2>

<h3>Overview</h3>
<p>
This lab demonstrates different ways to launch <strong>Amazon EC2</strong> instances. 
First, an EC2 instance is created using the <strong>AWS Management Console</strong> and used as a 
<strong>bastion host</strong>. Then, you connect to it securely with <strong>EC2 Instance Connect</strong> 
and use the <strong>AWS CLI</strong> to launch another EC2 instance that acts as a web server.
</p>

<h3>Architecture</h3>
<p>
A bastion host inside a VPC is used to securely access and create a web server EC2 instance.
</p>

<h3>Objectives</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Launch an EC2 instance using the AWS Management Console</li>
  <li>Connect to the EC2 instance using EC2 Instance Connect</li>
  <li>Launch another EC2 instance using the AWS CLI</li>
</ul>
